(:id "port/python/packet/if-else" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayout (both pinned interpreters, on its own fixture schema: the taken side round-trips, a read zeroes the untaken side to its zero values, not its defaults, SPEC §5, including the negated branch, and every proper prefix of both branches' wires is refused past_end at the first bit of the construct it stops in)" "internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayoutNegativeControl/untaken_zero (the untaken side's zeroing planted out of a copy of the generated reader and the probe goes red by name)" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_test.go: TestPythonBranchReadLocalsAreUnique (the branch reader and validator bind one typed local per temporary and round-trip both arms)" "make python-packet-layout-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "c37ce4ae4ba74b903ec06a8502f279c2ab4f1fb5" :note "2026-11-15: proved on the fixture only, run green on Linux x86_64 under the pinned CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current) with SCHEMA_SLOW=1: env SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -tags schema_leg_python -run TestPythonPacketLayout ./internal/codegen/python/, every test PASS, and the whole package green; the generated package is mypy --strict --python-version 3.11 clean. The goldens that use this construct (probe_header, bench_packet, bench_mixed, testdata) also use bits or other kinds carried by other packet cards, so they stay on the golden harness's skip list naming that kind until py-packet-close-r, which reads every golden with an empty skip list.")
(:id "port/python/packet/const" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayout (both pinned interpreters, on its own fixture schema: const(0xAB, 8) and a 36-bit const write their declared bytes and a read accepts them, a wrong const refuses as rejected at the bit after it, every cut inside the 36-bit const refuses past_end at bit 0, and a const wider than 32 bits rides the same path)" "internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayoutNegativeControl/const (the const comparison planted out of a copy of the generated reader and the probe goes red by name)" "internal/codegen/python/item_const.go" "make python-packet-layout-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "c37ce4ae4ba74b903ec06a8502f279c2ab4f1fb5" :note "2026-11-15: proved on the fixture only, run green on Linux x86_64 under the pinned CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current) with SCHEMA_SLOW=1: env SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -tags schema_leg_python -run TestPythonPacketLayout ./internal/codegen/python/, every test PASS, and the whole package green; the generated package is mypy --strict --python-version 3.11 clean. The goldens that use this construct (probe_header, bench_packet, bench_mixed, testdata) also use bits or other kinds carried by other packet cards, so they stay on the golden harness's skip list naming that kind until py-packet-close-r, which reads every golden with an empty skip list.")
(:id "port/python/packet/reserved" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayout (both pinned interpreters, on its own fixture schema: reserved(5) and reserved(40) write zero bits, a read refuses a set reserved bit in either as rejected at the bit after it, and every cut inside reserved(40) refuses past_end at bit 36)" "internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayoutNegativeControl/reserved (the reserved comparison planted out of a copy of the generated reader and the probe goes red by name)" "internal/codegen/python/item_reserved.go" "make python-packet-layout-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "c37ce4ae4ba74b903ec06a8502f279c2ab4f1fb5" :note "2026-11-15: proved on the fixture only, run green on Linux x86_64 under the pinned CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current) with SCHEMA_SLOW=1: env SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -tags schema_leg_python -run TestPythonPacketLayout ./internal/codegen/python/, every test PASS, and the whole package green; the generated package is mypy --strict --python-version 3.11 clean. The goldens that use this construct (probe_header, bench_packet, bench_mixed, testdata) also use bits or other kinds carried by other packet cards, so they stay on the golden harness's skip list naming that kind until py-packet-close-r, which reads every golden with an empty skip list.")
(:id "port/python/packet/align" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayout (both pinned interpreters, on its own fixture schema: align writes zero padding, a read refuses nonzero padding in either type and in a nested child as nonzero_padding at the byte boundary, and the following field reads at the aligned position; no byte prefix ends inside align padding, so every cut is pinned to the construct it stops in, and the set-padding cases are the align's hostile inputs)" "internal/codegen/python/python_layout_test.go: TestPythonPacketLayoutNegativeControl/align (the align read planted out of a copy of the generated reader and the probe goes red by name)" "internal/codegen/python/item_align.go" "make python-packet-layout-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "c37ce4ae4ba74b903ec06a8502f279c2ab4f1fb5" :note "2026-11-15: proved on the fixture only, run green on Linux x86_64 under the pinned CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current) with SCHEMA_SLOW=1: env SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -tags schema_leg_python -run TestPythonPacketLayout ./internal/codegen/python/, every test PASS, and the whole package green; the generated package is mypy --strict --python-version 3.11 clean. A byte prefix cannot end inside align padding (it pads to the next byte boundary), so the probe pins the cuts that bound the padding and refuses nonzero padding at the boundary in both types and in a nested child. The goldens that use this construct (probe_header, bench_packet, bench_mixed, testdata) also use bits or other kinds carried by other packet cards, so they stay on the golden harness's skip list naming that kind until py-packet-close-r, which reads every golden with an empty skip list.")
